    "summary": "A bedsheet, a &#039;pha lop&#039;; made of two equal sized pieces of natural cream tabby cotton cloth, with woven patterning at one end.  Bands of geometric patterning, 22 cms deep, including a line of black bird motifs.  The widest band has a line of confronted nagas (snakes), with bodies crossed.  Paterning worked in supplementary weft, &#039;khit&#039;, using red and black stranded cotton yarns.  Overhand knotting used to secure fringes.  Looser overhand knots used to group warp ends into tassels (macramé).  Unused.",
